um Corporation Limited (BPCL) today announced the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to collaborate on advancing the adoption of Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF) in India. The partnership marks an important step towards strengthening the country's SAF ecosystem and supports India's broader decarbonization ambitions, while aligning with global aviation sustainability frameworks including ICAO's CORSIA mandate.\n\nUnder the MoU, Akasa Air and BPCL have collaborated on establishing a framework for supply and offtake of SAF blended Aviation Turbine Fuel (ATF) at designated airports across India. The partnership will also focus on enabling long-term supply readiness by sharing indicative demand forecasts, supporting production planning and working towards a phased increase in SAF blending as the domestic ecosystem matures. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAkasa Air SkyCadet Programme: what it costs | Ready Aviator (https://readyaviator.com/cadet-pilot-programmes/akasa)\nciteturn276search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; In 2026, the Akasa Air cadet pilot programme costs ₹97.4 lakh to ₹1.06 croreReported, going by a capture of Akasa's own application FAQ, not independently confirmed.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPresenting the Akasa Air Anniversary Sale. Enjoy a range of offers on flight tickets. (https://www.akasaair.com/offers/anniversary-sale)\nciteturn276search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; •  December 24, 2025, up to 23:59 hours on January 4,2026 ... All Akasa Air flight bookings made under this Offer shall be subject to Akasa Air’s conditions of carriage available at www.akasaair.com.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBook Flight Tickets Online at the Lowest Prices Available | Akasa Air (https://www.akasaair.com/flight-booking)\nciteturn276search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; To g